"{\"url\":\"https://registry.isometric.com/project/prj_1K39D0N8S1S0TMKX\",\"title\":\"Kvina River CDR Project — Isometric\",\"head\":[\"VALIDATED\",\"MARINE\",\"1,000Y+\",\"Kvina River CDR Project\",\"CarbonRun\",\"ISSUED\",\"76.69\",\"BUFFER POOL\",\"1.534\",\"CREDITING PERIOD\",\"15 May 2025 to 15 May 2030\",\"Summary\"],\"issued_header\":\"76.69\",\"buffer_header\":\"1.534\",\"crediting\":\"15 May 2025 to 15 May 2030\",\"verifier\":\"350Solutions\",\"code\":\"XJ4Y\",\"approval\":\"20 Jan 2026\",\"protocol_current\":\"River Alkalinity Enhancement v1.0\",\"protocol_baseline\":null,\"cert_issued\":\"76.69\",\"cert_retired\":\"23.002\",\"cert_buffer\":\"1.534\",\"reversal\":\"The risk of reversal for this project has been assessed as very low. This means that 2% of certificates issued for this project are allocated to CarbonRun's buffer pool.\\n\\nTo date, this project has contributed 1.534 certificates to the buffer pool which holds a total of 1.534 certificates.\\n\\nCarbonRun has no reversals to date.\",\"showing\":[\"Showing 1 of 1\",\"Showing 4 of 4\",\"Showing 1 of 1\"],\"tables\":[{\"heads\":[\"Name\",\"Category\",\"Validated\"],\"rows\":[[\"Omya Biokalk 75\",\"Mineral & rock\",\"15 Jan 2026\"]]},{\"heads\":[\"Submission date\",\"Title\",\"Download\"],\"rows\":[[\"20 Jan 2026\",\"PDD\",\"PDF | ->\"],[\"20 Jan 2026\",\"Validation & Verification Report\",\"PDF | ->\"],[\"20 Jan 2026\",\"GHG Statement report\",\"PDF | ->\"],[\"03 Nov 2025\",\"Public Comment Summary\",\"PDF | ->\"]]},{\"heads\":[\"Issue date\",\"Issued\",\"Buffer pool\",\"Supplier allocation\"],\"rows\":[[\"20 Jan 2026\",\"76.69\",\"1.534\",\"75.156\"]]}],\"links\":[{\"h\":\"/supplier/spl_1JFW0WS9H1S0GKKN\",\"t\":\"CarbonRun\"},{\"h\":\"https://350solutions.com\",\"t\":\"350Solutions\"},{\"h\":\"/protocol/river-alkalinity-enhancement/1.0\",\"t\":\"River Alkalinity Enhancement v1.0\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1JFW0WS9H1S0GKKN/prj_1K39D0N8S1S0TMKX/pjd_1KZC3PSDW1S0WH5M/pdd.pdf\",\"t\":\"Project Design Document | 20 Jan 2026\"},{\"h\":\"/ghg-entry/rmv_1K72CKA4A1S0X6RP?tab=calculation-view\",\"t\":\"See GHG entry →\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1JFW0WS9H1S0GKKN/prj_1K39D0N8S1S0TMKX/pjd_1KZC3PSDW1S0WH5M/pdd.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1JFW0WS9H1S0GKKN/prj_1K39D0N8S1S0TMKX/pjd_1KFE20WQY1S0PD0Q/validation_%26_verification_report.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1JFW0WS9H1S0GKKN/prj_1K39D0N8S1S0TMKX/pjd_1KFDMK8BF1S0D88F/ghg_statement_report.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1JFW0WS9H1S0GKKN/prj_1K39D0N8S1S0TMKX/pjd_1KBYJWKVH1S0DFY6/public_comment_summary.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"}],\"text\":\"VALIDATED\\nMARINE\\n1,000Y+\\nKvina River CDR Project\\nCarbonRun\\nISSUED\\n76.69\\nBUFFER POOL\\n1.534\\nCREDITING PERIOD\\n15 May 2025 to 15 May 2030\\nSummary\\nRemoval method\\nCalculation overview\\nFeedstocks\\nProject documentation\\nCertificates\\nReversal risk\\nSummary\\n\\nKvina River CDR Project results in the drawdown and permanent storage of CO2 that would otherwise reside in the atmosphere. By adding finely crushed natural alkaline rock, the river’s pH, calcium, and total alkalinity are increased, strengthening ecosystem health and resilience in both the river and estuary. The alkaline material reacts with dissolved CO₂ to form stable bicarbonate ions, which increase the river’s dissolved inorganic carbon (DIC) load. As these bicarbonates flow to the ocean, they provide permanent, safe carbon storage for millennia while also improving water chemistry.\\n\\nPROJECT DETAILS\\nCurrent verifier\\n350Solutions\\n->\\nProject code\\nXJ4Y\\nApproval date\\n20 Jan 2026\\nCurrent protocol version\\nRiver Alkalinity Enhancement v1.0\\nSUSTAINABLE DEVELOPMENT GOALS\\n⌘ + scroll to zoom\\nKvina River CDR Project\\nHow carbon is being removed\\n\\nMarine carbon dioxide removal (mCDR) leverages the ocean's natural capacity to absorb and store carbon for thousands of years. These pathways use the biogeochemical and physical properties of the ocean and other bodies of water to capture carbon dioxide from the atmosphere or to permanently store carbon already contained within them. Approaches to mCDR include Ocean Alkalinity Enhancement and Direct Ocean Capture and Storage.\\n\\nProject Design Document\\n20 Jan 2026\\nCalculation overview\\nCalculations demonstrating 76.69 tCO₂e removed from Kvina River CDR Project on 15 Sep 2025\\nSee GHG entry →\\nNet CO₂e Removed\\n76.687 t\\nSequestrations\\n894.102 t\\n-\\nActivities\\n35.883 tCO₂e\\n+\\nCounterfactuals\\n748.220 t\\n+\\nUncertainty Discount\\n33.312 tCO₂e\\n⌘ + scroll to zoom\\nView full screen\\nFeedstocks\\n\\nFeedstocks are the validated input materials that have been used for this project.\\n\\nName\\tCategory\\tValidated\\nOmya Biokalk 75\\tMineral & rock\\t15 Jan 2026\\nShowing 1 of 1\\nPrevious\\nNext\\nProject documentation\\nSubmission date\\tTitle\\tDownload\\n20 Jan 2026\\tPDD\\tPDF\\n->\\n\\n20 Jan 2026\\tValidation & Verification Report\\tPDF\\n->\\n\\n20 Jan 2026\\tGHG Statement report\\tPDF\\n->\\n\\n03 Nov 2025\\tPublic Comment Summary\\tPDF\\n->\\nShowing 4 of 4\\nPrevious\\nNext\\nCertificates\\nIssued\\n76.69\\nRetired\\n23.002\\nBuffer pool\\n1.534\\nCrediting period\\n15 May 2025 to 15 May 2030\\nIssuances\\nRetirements\\nIssue date\\tIssued\\tBuffer pool\\tSupplier allocation\\n20 Jan 2026\\t76.69\\t1.534\\t75.156\\nShowing 1 of 1\\nPrevious\\nNext\\nReversal risk\\n\\nThe risk of reversal for this project has been assessed as very low. This means that 2% of certificates issued for this project are allocated to CarbonRun's buffer pool.\\n\\nTo date, this project has contributed 1.534 certificates to the buffer pool which holds a total of 1.534 certificates.\\n\\nCarbonRun has no reversals to date.\\n\\nLearn more about reversal risk\"}"